// =============================================================================
// PATIENT INVOICING
//
// ⚠️ THIS IS NOT `subscription_invoices`, AND THE TWO MUST NEVER BE MERGED.
//   `subscription_invoices` is RCLN billing the CLINIC for its SaaS
//   subscription: our GSTIN, the customer's location as the place of supply,
//   a gateway-driven lifecycle. These tables are the CLINIC billing a PATIENT:
//   the clinic's own GSTIN out of `issuer_tax_registrations`, the BRANCH as the
//   place of supply, a cashier-driven lifecycle, and branch-scoped RLS on top
//   of the tenant policy. Two issuers, two legal obligations, two tables. The
//   full comparison is §0.1 of `.kb/Architecture/invoice-engine-implementation.md`.
//
// PHI-ADJACENT, AND TREATED AS PHI.
//   An invoice names a patient and lists what was done to them — a line reading
//   "MRI Brain with contrast" is a clinical fact. Same rules as the PATIENTS
//   block above: allow-list snapshots into `audit_logs`, ids only in Redis and
//   in logs, never a name in a URL.
//
// WHAT IS AND IS NOT DECIDED HERE
//   Phase 3 is the data model. The arithmetic that fills the money columns is
//   Phase 4 (`packages/invoicing`, pure), and the lifecycle that defends them is
//   Phase 5 — landed, in `20260811090000_invoice_lifecycle_immutability`.
//
//   THREE TRIGGERS, WHICH `prisma migrate diff` CANNOT SEE AND WILL NOT WARN
//   YOU ABOUT. `invoices_lifecycle_guard` holds the transition table and freezes
//   every column of an ISSUED row except status, `amount_paid`, the
//   cancel/void fields and `updated_at`; `invoices_no_delete_after_issue` keeps
//   a numbered invoice in its series; `invoice_children_follow_parent` freezes
//   the lines and tax rows with the document that prints them. The frozen set is
//   an ALLOW-LIST, so a column added to this model tomorrow is immutable after
//   issue by default and somebody has to go and argue for it.
// =============================================================================

/// What the invoice was raised FOR. Drives the `{SOURCE}` segment of the number
/// and, from Phase 7, which invoices a caller is allowed to see at all.
///
/// ⚠️ THE ENUM IS COMPLETE; THE INTEGRATIONS ARE NOT.
///   `LAB`, `PHARMACY` and `INVENTORY` ship as values with nothing writing them,
///   because those modules do not exist yet (roadmap Phases 5 and 6). That is
///   deliberate: an enum value costs a migration to add later and nothing to
///   carry now, and shipping the shape means those modules land as integrations
///   rather than as a redesign of the invoice.
///
/// ⚠️ EACH SOURCE THAT EXISTS GETS ITS OWN COLUMN AND ITS OWN FOREIGN KEY.
///   There is deliberately NO generic `source_id`. A single polymorphic id
///   cannot be foreign-keyed anywhere, and — the part that actually matters —
///   the composite `(organization_id, id)` reference is what makes a
///   cross-tenant link unrepresentable (ADR-0004). A loose uuid would let an
///   invoice cite another clinic's appointment with nothing raising an error,
///   and the mitigation would be "the service remembers to re-read it", which is
///   the class of guarantee this schema exists to replace.
///
///   Stub tables holding just an id were considered and rejected: a link to a
///   table with no `organization_id` proves the row EXISTS and says nothing
///   about who it belongs to, which is the wrong half of the problem. Giving a
///   stub a tenant column makes it a half-designed `lab_orders` written with no
///   lab module behind it — plus an RLS policy and an isolation test for a table
///   that can never hold a row. The column and its FK arrive with the module, in
///   the migration that creates its table anyway.
///
///   `invoices_source_reference_matches_type` is the CHECK that keeps this enum
///   and the columns honest. It gains one clause per module.
enum InvoiceSourceType {
  /// A consultation. The only source integrated end to end today (Phase 8).
  APPOINTMENT
  /// A billable clinical procedure that is not a consultation.
  PROCEDURE
  /// Anything from the clinic's own service catalogue.
  SERVICE
  LAB
  PHARMACY
  INVENTORY
  /// A manual invoice typed by the cashier, citing nothing.
  OTHER
}

/// Is this document a charge or a reversal of one? (PI-8.)
///
/// ⚠️ A CREDIT NOTE IS AN INVOICE ROW WITH A DIFFERENT KIND, NOT A PARALLEL SET
///   OF TABLES, AND THAT IS THE LOAD-BEARING DECISION OF PI-8. The alternative —
///   `credit_notes` / `credit_note_items` / `credit_note_taxes` — duplicates the
///   line arithmetic, the apportionment, the tax snapshot, the document join and,
///   most of all, `invoices_lifecycle_guard`: the trigger that freezes an issued
///   document's every money column against an allow-list. That guard is the
///   hardest part of this engine to get right and the easiest to get subtly wrong
///   twice. A credit note has exactly the same immutability requirement, so it
///   gets exactly the same trigger by being the same table.
///
/// ⚠️ ITS SERIES IS SEPARATE, WHICH IS THE PART THE LAW ACTUALLY REQUIRES. Under
///   GST a credit note is its own document with its own consecutive number, so
///   `invoice-number.service.ts` keys it on a distinct period key and prints
///   `CRN-` rather than `INV-`. One table, two series — which is what a clinic's
///   books have always looked like.
///
/// ⚠️ AND EVERY QUERY THAT SUMS MONEY MUST SAY WHICH KIND IT MEANS. What a
///   patient owes is Σ INVOICE − Σ CREDIT_NOTE; the totals on a credit-note row
///   are POSITIVE and the KIND carries the sign, for the reason
///   `ChargeRequestKind` keeps the sign out of its quantity. A negative number in
///   a money column is one missing minus sign away from a credit that charges.
enum InvoiceKind {
  /// A charge. Every row written before PI-8 is one, which is why it is the
  /// default — the backfill for the existing table is the default itself.
  INVOICE
  /// A reversal of an issued invoice, in whole or in part. Cites the invoice it
  /// credits, and never edits it.
  CREDIT_NOTE
}

/// Where an invoice is in its life.
///
/// ⚠️ `DRAFT` IS THE ONLY STATE IN WHICH ANY MONEY COLUMN MAY MOVE. Everything
///   from ISSUED onwards is a document a patient has been handed and may have
///   claimed against insurance; a mistake is corrected with a credit note and a
///   new invoice, never by editing the totals of one already shown.
///   `invoices_lifecycle_guard` enforces that in the database rather than in the
///   service, and it is the transition table below as well: anything not on the
///   arrows is refused, including the ones that look harmless.
///
///     DRAFT ──▶ FINALIZING ──▶ ISSUED ──▶ PARTIALLY_PAID ──▶ PAID
///       │                        │              │             │
///       ▼                        └──────────────┴─────────────┴──▶ VOID
///     CANCELLED
enum InvoiceStatus {
  /// Being assembled. No number has been issued, so nothing here consumes a
  /// serial — an abandoned draft leaves no gap in the series.
  DRAFT
  /// The brief moment inside finalisation: the number has been taken and the
  /// totals frozen, but the transaction has not committed. A row observed in
  /// this state after a crash is a failed finalisation, not a lost invoice.
  FINALIZING
  /// Issued to the patient. Immutable from here.
  ISSUED
  /// Some money has arrived, and less than `grand_total` has.
  PARTIALLY_PAID
  PAID
  /// Abandoned before it was ever issued. Only reachable from DRAFT, which is
  /// what distinguishes it from VOID — nothing was ever shown to anybody, so
  /// there is nothing to reverse and no credit note to raise.
  CANCELLED
  /// Issued and then reversed. The row and its number stay for ever: voiding is
  /// how a series stays contiguous when a document has to be undone. A void
  /// that involved money also produces a credit note.
  VOID
}

/// How a discount was expressed by whoever entered it.
///
/// The INPUT is kept alongside the computed amount because "10% off" and "₹150
/// off" print differently and are re-derivable from each other only by knowing
/// which one was typed.
enum InvoiceDiscountType {
  /// Basis points, in `discount_bps`. 10% is 1000.
  PERCENTAGE
  /// A currency amount, in `discount_fixed`.
  FIXED
}

/// One patient invoice.
///
/// ⚠️ `invoice_number` IS NULL UNTIL FINALISATION, AND THAT IS THE POINT.
///   The number comes from `issueNumber()`, whose row lock is held to COMMIT, so
///   it is taken as late as possible — at finalisation, not at creation. A draft
///   the cashier abandons therefore burns no serial. See §0.6 of the
///   implementation log for the scope decision behind the format.
///
/// ⚠️ THE NUMBER'S SERIES IS PER BRANCH, AND THE BRANCH CODE IS IN THE NUMBER.
///   `INV-{PERIOD_YEAR}-{SOURCE}-{BRANCH_CODE}-{000001}`. The branch segment is
///   not decoration: GST requires a serial that is consecutive and unique per
///   ISSUER, and the issuer is the GSTIN, which in India is per state. A
///   per-branch counter without a per-branch discriminator gives two branches
///   sharing one GSTIN two different invoices both numbered
///   `INV-2026-APP-000001`, which is the one thing the series may not do.
///   Multiple series under one registration are allowed; a repeated number is
///   not. Branch codes are org-unique, so the whole string is too.
///
/// ⚠️ EVERY TAX FIELD BELOW IS A SNAPSHOT AND IS NEVER RE-READ.
///   Registrations lapse, rates change by statute, and a branch's `region_code`
///   gets corrected. An invoice that recomputed itself from today's
///   configuration would silently restate a document somebody has already filed
///   a return on. What was true at issue is what stays on the row.
model Invoice {
  id             String  @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  organizationId String  @map("organization_id") @db.Uuid
  /// NOT NULL: the branch is the place of supply, the number series and the RLS
  /// boundary. An invoice with no branch could not be taxed or numbered.
  branchId       String  @map("branch_id") @db.Uuid
  /// Null while DRAFT. See the header.
  invoiceNumber  String? @map("invoice_number") @db.VarChar(64)

  /// A charge, or a reversal of one (PI-8). See `InvoiceKind`.
  kind InvoiceKind @default(INVOICE)
  /// The issued invoice this credit note reverses. Set iff `kind` is
  /// `CREDIT_NOTE`, by CHECK, and composite-FK'd so a clinic can never credit
  /// another clinic's document.
  ///
  /// ⚠️ NOT UNIQUE, FOR THE REASON `appointment_id` IS NOT. A partly returned
  ///   supply is credited twice as the rest comes back, and both notes cite the
  ///   same invoice. "How much of this invoice has been credited?" is a SUM, and
  ///   the engine refuses a note that would take that sum past the invoice's own
  ///   `grand_total`.
  creditedInvoiceId String? @map("credited_invoice_id") @db.Uuid

  /// What kind of thing this invoice bills for. The discriminator over the
  /// typed reference columns below — see the enum's header.
  sourceType    InvoiceSourceType @map("source_type")
  /// The visit this invoice bills for. Set iff `sourceType` is APPOINTMENT, and
  /// composite-FK'd, so an invoice can never bill another clinic's appointment.
  ///
  /// The first of what will be one column per integrated source: `labOrderId`
  /// arrives with the lab module, each in the migration that creates its own
  /// table. PROCEDURE, SERVICE and OTHER carry no reference at all — a manual
  /// invoice cites nothing, and the service catalogue those first two will point
  /// at does not exist either.
  ///
  /// ⚠️ `PHARMACY` AND `INVENTORY` DELIBERATELY GAINED NO COLUMN HERE IN PI-8,
  ///   AND THAT IS NOT THE RULE ABOVE BEING BENT. This comment used to promise a
  ///   `pharmacySaleId`, and building one would have been wrong: a pharmacy
  ///   invoice bills a SET of supplies, not one. Three dispenses across a
  ///   morning are routinely one bill, and an inpatient's are one at discharge —
  ///   a single id could name only the first of them, and the rest would be
  ///   billed on a document that cites nothing.
  ///
  ///   The link exists and is stronger for being on the other side:
  ///   `charge_requests.invoice_id` is many-to-one and composite-FK'd to BOTH
  ///   the invoice and the dispense line, so the tenant travels in both keys and
  ///   a cross-tenant reference stays unrepresentable (ADR-0004) — which is the
  ///   guarantee this rule exists to preserve, not the column shape.
  ///   `invoices_source_reference_matches_type` therefore needs no new clause,
  ///   because a pharmacy invoice carries no reference column to constrain.
  ///
  /// ⚠️ NOT UNIQUE, DELIBERATELY. A visit billed, voided and billed again has
  ///   two invoices citing it, and the void must keep its reference or the
  ///   correction cannot be explained. "Is this visit already billed?" is a
  ///   question about the LIVE invoice, which is a lifecycle concern (Phase 5)
  ///   rather than a uniqueness one.
  appointmentId String?           @map("appointment_id") @db.Uuid

  /// Null for a walk-in customer with no record — a supplier's rep buying a
  /// consumable, or a bill raised to a company. Composite-FK'd when present, so
  /// an invoice can never name another tenant's patient.
  patientId String? @map("patient_id") @db.Uuid

  /// ⚠️ THE CUSTOMER BLOCK IS A SNAPSHOT, NOT A JOIN, AND THAT IS NOT
  ///   DENORMALISATION FOR SPEED. A patient marries and changes their surname;
  ///   an address is corrected. The invoice must keep printing what it printed,
  ///   because the copy in the patient's file and the copy in the clinic's
  ///   records have to agree years later. `patient_id` is the link for querying;
  ///   these columns are the document.
  customerName    String  @map("customer_name") @db.VarChar(255)
  customerPhone   String? @map("customer_phone") @db.VarChar(20)
  customerEmail   String? @map("customer_email") @db.VarChar(255)
  customerAddress String? @map("customer_address") @db.Text
  /// The customer's own GSTIN/VAT number, on the rare invoice raised to a
  /// business. Passed to the engine as UNVALIDATED — nothing checks it.
  customerTaxId   String? @map("customer_tax_id") @db.VarChar(32)

  /// WHO PROVIDED THE CARE THIS INVOICE BILLS.
  ///
  /// A bill for a consultation that does not name the clinician is a receipt for
  /// an unattributed service: the patient cannot claim it, an insurer will not
  /// accept it, and the clinic cannot answer "who saw them?" from the document.
  ///
  /// ⚠️ SNAPSHOTTED FOR EXACTLY THE REASON THE CUSTOMER BLOCK ABOVE IS. A doctor
  ///   leaves the clinic, changes their name, or renews under a new council
  ///   number — and the invoices they were named on must go on saying what they
  ///   said. `appointment_id` is the link for querying; these are the document.
  ///   Nothing in the template joins to `appointments` or `doctor_profiles`.
  ///
  /// Null on every source that is not a consultation. A pharmacy dispense has a
  /// PRESCRIBER, which is a different fact deserving its own column when that
  /// module exists — putting it here would print "attended by" on a bill for a
  /// box of tablets nobody was attended for.
  practitionerName               String? @map("practitioner_name") @db.VarChar(255)
  /// Their registration with their council, printed under the name where they
  /// hold one. Read from `doctor_profiles.registration_number` at billing time.
  practitionerRegistrationNumber String? @map("practitioner_registration_number") @db.VarChar(64)
  /// WHO THIS INVOICE BELONGS TO, FOR QUERYING. The live link, where the two
  /// columns above are the printed document — exactly the split between
  /// `patient_id` and `customer_name`.
  ///
  /// ⚠️ IT IS A VISIBILITY BOUNDARY AND NOT A CONVENIENCE. A doctor holds
  ///   `billing.invoice.read` and not `.read_all`, and sees the invoices for the
  ///   care THEY gave — this column is what that filter runs on, in the query
  ///   rather than in a route guard. Reading it off the appointment through a
  ///   join would work today and stop working the moment a lab or pharmacy
  ///   invoice has an ordering clinician and no appointment.
  ///
  /// Null on anything nobody attended: a counter sale, a manual invoice.
  practitionerProfileId          String? @map("practitioner_profile_id") @db.Uuid

  /// ⚠️ THE DATE OF SUPPLY, WHICH IS NOT `issued_at` AND NOT `now()`.
  ///   It is what selects the effective-dated tax rule and the registration, so
  ///   an invoice raised in April for a consultation given in March is taxed as
  ///   March was. Every caller passes it explicitly; `loadTaxContext(at)` is
  ///   handed this value and nothing else.
  suppliedAt DateTime  @map("supplied_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)
  /// When it became a document. Null until then, and the pair with
  /// `invoice_number` — both are set by finalisation or neither is.
  issuedAt   DateTime? @map("issued_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)
  dueDate    DateTime? @map("due_date") @db.Date

  /// Which of the clinic's registrations this was issued under. Composite-FK'd,
  /// so an invoice can never be raised under another tenant's GSTIN. Null when
  /// the clinic holds none covering the branch — a legal position, not an
  /// error, and the reason `tax_treatment` has a NOT_REGISTERED value.
  issuerTaxRegistrationId String?      @map("issuer_tax_registration_id") @db.Uuid
  /// The registration number as printed. Snapshotted beside the id because the
  /// row it came from can be corrected and this string may not change.
  issuerTaxId             String?      @map("issuer_tax_id") @db.VarChar(64)
  /// The legal name the registration is held in, which is not always the name
  /// over the door. A GST invoice must print the registered name.
  issuerLegalName         String?      @map("issuer_legal_name") @db.VarChar(255)
  /// Where this supply was deemed to take place — `IN-KA`, `AE`. The BRANCH's
  /// jurisdiction, never the patient's address. Getting this backwards bills a
  /// Karnataka consultation for a Kerala patient as inter-state: IGST instead of
  /// CGST+SGST, and the state's half never reaches the state.
  placeOfSupply           String?      @map("place_of_supply") @db.VarChar(10)
  /// The document-level position, which is the worst of its lines: one UNRATED
  /// line makes the whole invoice unissuable. `isIssuable()` in `@rcln/tax` is
  /// the single definition, so this column and the engine cannot drift.
  taxTreatment            TaxTreatment @default(NOT_REGISTERED) @map("tax_treatment")

  currency String @default("INR") @db.Char(3)

  /// Σ line gross, before any discount. The order every column below is computed
  /// in is fixed in §0.5 of the implementation log and implemented once, in
  /// Phase 4's `priceInvoice`.
  subtotal             Decimal              @default(0) @db.Decimal(14, 2)
  /// Σ per-line discounts.
  lineDiscountTotal    Decimal              @default(0) @map("line_discount_total") @db.Decimal(14, 2)
  /// The invoice-level discount AS ENTERED. Null means none.
  discountType         InvoiceDiscountType? @map("discount_type")
  /// Set iff `discount_type` is PERCENTAGE. Basis points, so the input stays an
  /// integer. Enforced by CHECK — the two input columns and the type agree or
  /// the row does not go in.
  discountBps          Int?                 @map("discount_bps")
  /// Set iff `discount_type` is FIXED.
  discountFixed        Decimal?             @map("discount_fixed") @db.Decimal(14, 2)
  /// What the invoice-level discount came to once apportioned.
  ///
  /// ⚠️ APPORTIONED ACROSS THE LINES BEFORE TAX, NOT SUBTRACTED AFTER IT.
  ///   A discount that reduces what the customer pays reduces the taxable value
  ///   of the supply. Tax computed on the pre-discount amount is over-collected
  ///   tax, remitted to an authority on money nobody ever received. The split is
  ///   pro-rata by taxable amount, largest-remainder so the parts sum to the
  ///   whole exactly, and it lands in `invoice_items.apportioned_discount`. This
  ///   is a deliberate deviation from the original brief's §7 sketch.
  invoiceDiscountTotal Decimal              @default(0) @map("invoice_discount_total") @db.Decimal(14, 2)
  /// Σ line taxable — what tax was actually computed on.
  taxableAmount        Decimal              @default(0) @map("taxable_amount") @db.Decimal(14, 2)
  /// Σ every `invoice_taxes` row. Rounded PER LINE, not per invoice: the two
  /// differ by up to (n−1) minor units, and per-line is what a GST invoice does
  /// and what makes each printed line internally consistent.
  taxTotal             Decimal              @default(0) @map("tax_total") @db.Decimal(14, 2)
  /// Cash rounding to the nearest note, where a clinic does that. Signed, and
  /// kept as its own column so `grand_total` never has to be explained.
  roundingAdjustment   Decimal              @default(0) @map("rounding_adjustment") @db.Decimal(14, 2)
  grandTotal           Decimal              @default(0) @map("grand_total") @db.Decimal(14, 2)
  /// Settled so far. The balance is `grand_total − amount_paid` and is
  /// deliberately NOT a column: a stored balance is a third number that can
  /// disagree with the two it is derived from.
  amountPaid           Decimal              @default(0) @map("amount_paid") @db.Decimal(14, 2)

  status InvoiceStatus @default(DRAFT)

  /// ⚠️ PHI-CAPABLE FREE TEXT, printed on the invoice. In `REDACTED_KEYS`.
  notes              String? @db.Text
  /// Why it was cancelled or voided. Same PHI treatment as `notes`.
  cancellationReason String? @map("cancellation_reason") @db.Text

  createdBy   String?   @map("created_by") @db.Uuid
  /// Who finalised it. The accountable act — a draft's editor is in audit_logs.
  issuedBy    String?   @map("issued_by") @db.Uuid
  cancelledBy String?   @map("cancelled_by") @db.Uuid
  cancelledAt DateTime? @map("cancelled_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)
  voidedAt    DateTime? @map("voided_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)

  createdAt DateTime  @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)
  updatedAt DateTime  @updatedAt @map("updated_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)
  /// Soft delete for a DRAFT only. An issued invoice is never deleted by any
  /// path — it is VOIDed, which keeps the number and the trail.
  deletedAt DateTime? @map("deleted_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)

  organization       Organization           @relation(fields: [organizationId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  branch             Branch                 @relation(fields: [organizationId, branchId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Cascade)
  patient            Patient?               @relation(fields: [organizationId, patientId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Restrict)
  /// Restrict: a visit that has been billed cannot be deleted out from under its
  /// invoice. Appointments are soft-deleted anyway, so this only ever fires on a
  /// hard delete somebody meant to be harmless.
  appointment        Appointment?           @relation(fields: [organizationId, appointmentId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: NoAction)
  /// Restrict: a registration that priced issued invoices cannot be deleted out
  /// from under them. `effective_to` is how a registration is retired.
  issuerRegistration IssuerTaxRegistration? @relation(fields: [organizationId, issuerTaxRegistrationId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: NoAction)
  /// Composite FK, per ADR-0004: the tenant travels in the key, so an invoice can
  /// never be attributed to another clinic's clinician.
  ///
  /// Restrict, like `appointment` above and for the same reason — a clinician
  /// whose work has been billed cannot be hard-deleted out from under the
  /// invoices that name them. Doctor profiles are soft-deleted anyway, so this
  /// only ever fires on a delete somebody meant to be harmless. (`SetNull` is not
  /// available: the key includes `organization_id`, which is NOT NULL.)
  practitioner       DoctorProfile?         @relation("InvoicePractitioner", fields: [organizationId, practitionerProfileId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: NoAction)
  creator            User?                  @relation("InvoiceCreatedBy", fields: [createdBy], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)
  issuer             User?                  @relation("InvoiceIssuedBy", fields: [issuedBy], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)
  canceller          User?                  @relation("InvoiceCancelledBy", fields: [cancelledBy], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)

  /// The document this one credits, and the notes credited against it (PI-8).
  creditedInvoice Invoice?  @relation("InvoiceCreditNote", fields: [organizationId, creditedInvoiceId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: NoAction)
  creditNotes     Invoice[] @relation("InvoiceCreditNote")

  items     InvoiceItem[]
  taxes     InvoiceTax[]
  documents InvoiceDocument[]
  /// What this invoice billed (PI-8). Written by `services/invoicing` on the
  /// charge request, never the other way round.
  chargeRequests ChargeRequest[]

  /// ⚠️ THE ONE UNIQUE IN THIS SCHEMA THAT WANTS NULLS **DISTINCT**, WHICH IS
  ///   POSTGRES' DEFAULT — so it is written plainly and this comment exists
  ///   because CONVENTIONS.md says every nullable unique gets NULLS NOT
  ///   DISTINCT. Here the opposite is required: every DRAFT has a NULL
  ///   `invoice_number`, and a clinic has many drafts open at once. NULLS NOT
  ///   DISTINCT would let it hold exactly one.
  ///
  ///   Org-wide rather than per branch, which is STRONGER than the legal
  ///   requirement and safe because the branch code is inside the string.
  @@unique([organizationId, invoiceNumber])
  /// Composite-FK target for items, taxes and documents (ADR-0004).
  @@unique([organizationId, id])
  /// The invoice list: one branch, newest first, filtered by state.
  @@index([organizationId, branchId, status, createdAt])
  /// "What does this patient owe?" — and the ledger on the patient page.
  @@index([organizationId, patientId, createdAt])
  /// "Has this appointment been billed?", asked once per row on the day board.
  @@index([organizationId, appointmentId])
  /// A clinician's own list, and "what did Dr Rao bill this month".
  ///
  /// ⚠️ THIS LINE IS THE FIX FOR A DRIFT BUG, NOT A NEW INDEX. The index was
  ///   created by the `invoice_practitioner_scope` migration and never declared
  ///   here, so `prisma migrate dev` emitted a `DROP INDEX` for it into the NEXT
  ///   unrelated migration anybody generated — and did so silently, because a
  ///   dropped index breaks no test and no type. Declaring it makes the diff
  ///   empty. If you add a hand-written index in a migration, add it here too.
  @@index([organizationId, practitionerProfileId])
  /// "What has been credited against this invoice?" — asked once per credit
  /// note to check the running sum, and once per invoice detail render.
  @@index([organizationId, creditedInvoiceId])
  @@map("invoices")
}

/// One billable line.
///
/// ⚠️ CARRIES ITS OWN `organization_id` AND `branch_id` RATHER THAN HANGING OFF
///   THE INVOICE, and that is a security decision rather than a convenience.
///   Its parent is BRANCH-scoped. A child with no tenant columns can only be
///   protected by a policy that reaches into the parent, and such a policy
///   evaluates with row security DISABLED on the table it reads — so the branch
///   half has to be restated by hand, exactly as `appointment_status_history`
///   was forced to. Carrying both columns makes this an ordinary member of both
///   RLS loops instead, which is the same call `appointment_vitals` made and for
///   the same reason. The service copies both from the invoice; the composite FK
///   is what stops them disagreeing.
///
/// ⚠️ NO `deleted_at`, DELIBERATELY. A line is hard-deleted while the invoice is
///   DRAFT and cannot be touched afterwards. A soft-deleted line is a row that
///   every total in Phase 4 must remember to exclude, and the first query that
///   forgets prices an invoice that does not match its own printout.
model InvoiceItem {
  id             String @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  organizationId String @map("organization_id") @db.Uuid
  branchId       String @map("branch_id") @db.Uuid
  invoiceId      String @map("invoice_id") @db.Uuid

  /// Print order, 1-based. Explicit rather than implied by `created_at`,
  /// because a cashier reorders lines and a reprint must match the original.
  lineNumber  Int     @map("line_number") @db.SmallInt
  description String  @db.VarChar(255)
  /// The HSN/SAC code printed on the line. Presentation only — `tax_category`
  /// is what actually selects the rate, and the two are separate so a clinic can
  /// print a code without that string silently becoming a lookup key.
  itemCode    String? @map("item_code") @db.VarChar(32)
  /// The line on the ORIGINAL invoice that this credit-note line reverses
  /// (PI-8, closing the per-line half of the credit ceiling).
  ///
  /// ⚠️ WITHOUT IT THE PER-LINE CAP CANNOT AGGREGATE, AND THAT WAS A REAL
  ///   DEFECT. `resolveLines` caps a credited quantity against the ORIGINAL
  ///   line's quantity; with no link back there was nothing to sum across
  ///   earlier notes, so a two-line bill could be credited twice on line A and
  ///   never on line B. The total stayed bounded by `assertWithinRemaining`, so
  ///   no clinic could refund more than it charged — but the document said more
  ///   of A came back than ever went out, and stock reconciliation reads lines.
  ///
  /// ⚠️ SET ONLY ON A `CREDIT_NOTE`'s LINES, AND **NOT** ENFORCED BY A CHECK.
  ///   The constraint it wants is "non-null only when the parent invoice's
  ///   `kind` is CREDIT_NOTE", which is a fact about ANOTHER ROW and therefore
  ///   not expressible as a CHECK. A trigger was considered and refused: this is
  ///   provenance rather than a money column, the service is its only writer,
  ///   and the cost of getting it wrong is a broken link rather than a wrong
  ///   figure. Recorded so nobody assumes the database is holding it.
  ///
  /// ⚠️ IT MUST SURVIVE A REPRICE. `repriceLoadedDraft` DELETES and re-inserts
  ///   every line, so this column is carried through `StagedLine` — the same
  ///   trap that made `charge_requests.invoice_item_id` unusable and got that
  ///   column removed. The credit note is finalised, and finalisation re-prices.
  ///
  /// Composite-FK'd, so a note can never cite another clinic's invoice line.
  creditedInvoiceItemId String? @map("credited_invoice_item_id") @db.Uuid

  /// ⚠️ THE KEY INTO `tax_rules`, MATCHED EXACTLY. There is no HSN prefix tree,
  ///   deliberately: a prefix match that resolved `30049099` to the broader
  ///   `3004` heading would apply a confident, unreviewed rate. A category with
  ///   no rule comes back UNRATED and Phase 5 refuses to issue the invoice.
  taxCategory String  @map("tax_category") @db.VarChar(64)

  /// Decimal(14,3): half a tablet is real, and so is 0.5 hours of physiotherapy.
  quantity  Decimal @default(1) @db.Decimal(14, 3)
  unitPrice Decimal @map("unit_price") @db.Decimal(14, 2)

  /// round(unit_price × quantity). Stored rather than derived because every
  /// later column is computed from the ROUNDED value, and re-deriving it in a
  /// query would reintroduce the fraction the rounding removed.
  grossAmount         Decimal              @map("gross_amount") @db.Decimal(14, 2)
  /// The line's own discount, as entered. Same three-column shape and same
  /// CHECK as the invoice.
  discountType        InvoiceDiscountType? @map("discount_type")
  discountBps         Int?                 @map("discount_bps")
  discountFixed       Decimal?             @map("discount_fixed") @db.Decimal(14, 2)
  discountAmount      Decimal              @default(0) @map("discount_amount") @db.Decimal(14, 2)
  /// This line's share of the INVOICE-level discount, pro-rata by taxable
  /// amount with the remainder distributed largest-first. Kept apart from
  /// `discount_amount` so the printed line can show the discount the customer
  /// asked for separately from the one the whole bill got.
  apportionedDiscount Decimal              @default(0) @map("apportioned_discount") @db.Decimal(14, 2)
  /// gross − discount − apportioned. What tax is computed on.
  taxableAmount       Decimal              @map("taxable_amount") @db.Decimal(14, 2)
  /// Σ this line's `invoice_taxes` rows.
  taxAmount           Decimal              @default(0) @map("tax_amount") @db.Decimal(14, 2)
  lineTotal           Decimal              @map("line_total") @db.Decimal(14, 2)

  /// Why this line was taxed the way it was, per line and not per invoice: a
  /// bill can carry an EXEMPT consultation and a STANDARD-rated medicine.
  taxTreatment TaxTreatment @default(UNRATED) @map("tax_treatment")
  /// The engine's own explanation, printed on the invoice where a jurisdiction
  /// requires one ("Healthcare services — exempt under Notification 12/2017").
  /// ⚠️ Never a message built for a developer: this reaches a patient.
  taxReason    String?      @map("tax_reason") @db.VarChar(255)

  createdAt DateTime @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt @map("updated_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)

  organization Organization @relation(fields: [organizationId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  branch       Branch       @relation(fields: [organizationId, branchId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Cascade)
  invoice      Invoice      @relation(fields: [organizationId, invoiceId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Cascade)

  taxes InvoiceTax[]

  /// Restrict: an issued invoice's lines are frozen, so the row a credit note
  /// cites cannot move under it. A DRAFT's lines are deleted on every reprice,
  /// and a credit note only ever cites an ISSUED invoice — which is what makes
  /// Restrict safe rather than a landmine.
  creditedItem  InvoiceItem?  @relation("InvoiceItemCredit", fields: [organizationId, creditedInvoiceItemId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: NoAction)
  creditedBy    InvoiceItem[] @relation("InvoiceItemCredit")

  /// Composite-FK target so `invoice_taxes` can cite the line it priced.
  @@unique([organizationId, id])
  /// Two lines cannot claim the same position on one document.
  @@unique([organizationId, invoiceId, lineNumber])
  /// "How much of this line has already been credited?" — summed per line across
  /// every live note, on every credit note raised.
  @@index([organizationId, creditedInvoiceItemId])
  @@map("invoice_items")
}

/// One PRINTED tax line on one invoice item.
///
/// ⚠️ A RATE AND A LINE ARE NOT THE SAME THING, WHICH IS WHY THIS TABLE IS PER
///   LINE AND NOT PER RATE. 12% in Karnataka prints as two rows of 6% owed to
///   two different governments; the same 12% in Singapore prints as one; British
///   Columbia prints two rows at two different rates. The arithmetic is
///   identical and only the presentation differs, so the presentation is data —
///   `@rcln/tax` decides it, and this table records what it decided.
///
/// ⚠️ EVERYTHING HERE IS SNAPSHOTTED, INCLUDING THE NAME. Rates change by
///   statute and a rule can be retired. `name` is what the authority calls it,
///   printed verbatim: a line reading "Tax" is compliant nowhere.
model InvoiceTax {
  id             String @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  organizationId String @map("organization_id") @db.Uuid
  branchId       String @map("branch_id") @db.Uuid
  /// Denormalised from the item so the invoice's tax summary is one indexed
  /// read rather than a join through every line.
  invoiceId      String @map("invoice_id") @db.Uuid
  invoiceItemId  String @map("invoice_item_id") @db.Uuid

  /// Which rule priced this line, for the auditor who asks why.
  ///
  /// ⚠️ EXACTLY ONE OF THE TWO IS SET, ENFORCED BY CHECK — a rate resolves
  ///   either from the clinic's own `tax_rules` or, inherited, from rcln's
  ///   `tax_rule_defaults`, and which one it was is the difference between "the
  ///   clinic chose this" and "the clinic accepted our published default".
  ///   Collapsing them into one nullable id would destroy that distinction, and
  ///   it is the distinction the rate-card screen exists to show. Both are NULL
  ///   only where no rule was involved at all: an UNRATED or NOT_REGISTERED
  ///   line, or a rate that came from an external tax provider.
  taxRuleId        String? @map("tax_rule_id") @db.Uuid
  taxRuleDefaultId String? @map("tax_rule_default_id") @db.Uuid

  /// `CGST`, `SGST`, `IGST`, `VAT`, `HST`, `PST`, `Consumption Tax`.
  name          String       @db.VarChar(32)
  /// Which authority it is owed to — `IN` for CGST, `IN-KA` for SGST. One supply
  /// carrying two lines to two governments is exactly what a GST split is, and
  /// without this column the two halves are indistinguishable on a return.
  jurisdiction  String?      @db.VarChar(10)
  /// Basis points, snapshotted. 6% is 600.
  rateBps       Int          @map("rate_bps")
  /// What this rate was applied to. Equal to the item's `taxable_amount` for
  /// every rule this engine computes, and NOT redundant: a stacked provincial
  /// tax elsewhere may be levied on a different base, and a provider quote
  /// supplies its own.
  taxableAmount Decimal      @map("taxable_amount") @db.Decimal(14, 2)
  taxAmount     Decimal      @map("tax_amount") @db.Decimal(14, 2)
  treatment     TaxTreatment

  createdAt DateTime @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)

  organization   Organization    @relation(fields: [organizationId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  branch         Branch          @relation(fields: [organizationId, branchId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Cascade)
  invoice        Invoice         @relation(fields: [organizationId, invoiceId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Cascade)
  item           InvoiceItem     @relation(fields: [organizationId, invoiceItemId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Cascade, onUpdate: NoAction)
  /// Restrict on both: the row that explains a charge outlives the screen that
  /// created it. A rate is withdrawn with `effective_to`, never a DELETE.
  taxRule        TaxRule?        @relation(fields: [organizationId, taxRuleId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: NoAction)
  taxRuleDefault TaxRuleDefault? @relation(fields: [taxRuleDefaultId], references: [id], onDelete: Restrict)

  @@index([organizationId, invoiceId])
  @@index([organizationId, invoiceItemId])
  @@map("invoice_taxes")
}

/// The join between an invoice and a file in `files`.
///
/// A separate table rather than a `file_id` column on `invoices` because one
/// invoice legitimately has several documents over its life — the invoice PDF, a
/// credit note against it, a reprint after a FAILED render — and the current one
/// of each kind has to be findable without the invoice row growing a column per
/// document type.
///
/// ⚠️ `file_id` IS A PLAIN FK, NOT THE COMPOSITE ONE ADR-0004 ASKS FOR.
///   `files.organization_id` is NULLABLE — platform assets live in the same
///   table — so a composite FK from a NOT NULL column cannot reference it. The
///   tenant guarantee is therefore restored in the policy layer instead: a
///   RESTRICTIVE `file_in_same_org` policy in enable-rls.sql, written the same
///   way `invitation_branches.branch_in_same_org` was and for the same reason.
///   Removing that policy silently re-opens a cross-tenant reference.
model InvoiceDocument {
  id             String       @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  organizationId String       @map("organization_id") @db.Uuid
  branchId       String       @map("branch_id") @db.Uuid
  invoiceId      String       @map("invoice_id") @db.Uuid
  fileId         String       @map("file_id") @db.Uuid
  documentType   DocumentType @map("document_type")

  /// Which template drew it, and which revision of that template.
  ///
  /// ⚠️ PROVENANCE, NOT A FEATURE FLAG. Nothing reads these back to choose a
  ///   renderer — an issued invoice's PDF is generated once and never
  ///   regenerated, so there is no code path that could. They exist so that
  ///   "what did the document this patient is holding actually look like?" has
  ///   an answer years later, when the template has moved on several revisions
  ///   and the only copy of the old one is in the git history. Without them the
  ///   stored bytes are the sole record of their own layout, which is fine until
  ///   the question is about a document somebody has disputed.
  ///
  ///   `@rcln/documents` owns both values — `INVOICE_TEMPLATE_KEY` and
  ///   `INVOICE_TEMPLATE_VERSION`. A second document type takes a new KEY; a
  ///   change to how this one looks bumps the VERSION.
  templateKey     String @map("template_key") @db.VarChar(64)
  templateVersion Int    @map("template_version") @db.SmallInt

  generatedAt  DateTime  @default(now()) @map("generated_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)
  generatedBy  String?   @map("generated_by") @db.Uuid
  /// Set when a newer document of the same kind replaces this one — which can
  /// only happen for a render that FAILED. An issued invoice's PDF is immutable,
  /// so a corrected invoice is a credit note plus a new invoice, never a version
  /// 2 of this file.
  supersededAt DateTime? @map("superseded_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)

  createdAt DateTime @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)

  organization Organization @relation(fields: [organizationId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  branch       Branch       @relation(fields: [organizationId, branchId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Cascade)
  invoice      Invoice      @relation(fields: [organizationId, invoiceId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Cascade)
  /// Restrict: nothing may delete the PDF an issued invoice points at. There is
  /// deliberately no `deleteDocument` in DocumentService either.
  file         StoredFile   @relation(fields: [fileId], references: [id], onDelete: Restrict)
  generator    User?        @relation("InvoiceDocumentGeneratedBy", fields: [generatedBy], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)

  /// ⚠️ THE "ONE CURRENT DOCUMENT PER TYPE" UNIQUE IS **NOT DECLARED HERE**, and
  ///   that is deliberate. It is PARTIAL — `WHERE superseded_at IS NULL` — which
  ///   Prisma cannot express, and a declared total unique would both be a lie
  ///   about the shape and make `migrate diff` propose renaming the real index
  ///   on every run. It is created by hand in the migration as
  ///   `invoice_documents_current_per_type_key`, the same treatment the
  ///   expression trigram index on `patients` gets. A non-partial unique would
  ///   refuse the retry after a FAILED render, which is the exact case
  ///   `superseded_at` exists to allow.
  @@index([organizationId, invoiceId])
  @@index([organizationId, fileId])
  @@map("invoice_documents")
}
